Active Text\n- **Name:** gatsby\n- **Attempt:** 3 of 5\n- **Phase:** awaiting_evaluation\n- **baseline_score:** 6.20\n\n## Output Files\n- HTML: output/gatsby/report.html\n- JSON: output/gatsby/analysis.json\n- Quality Report: output/gatsby_20260118_124832/quality.md\n\n## Pipeline Notes (Attempt 3)\n- Analysis completed in 64m 16s\n- Total tokens: 698,614\n- Narrator detected: Mrs. Sigourney Howard (CRITICAL ISSUE - still wrong)\n- 60 characters extracted\n- 9 chapters detected\n- Warnings:\n  - TOC validation: 87 entries seems too many\n  - StructureAgent: 2 errors found but refinement not yet implemented\n  - 4 low-confidence character profiles (McKee, Catherine, the butler, Mrs. McKee)\n  - Multiple moral valence classification failures\n  - Multiple JSON parsing failures for character profiles","newString":"## Active Text\n- **Name:** gatsby\n- **Attempt:** 4 of 5\n- **Phase:** awaiting_evaluation\n- **baseline_score:** 6.20\n\n## Output Files\n- HTML: output/gatsby/report.html\n- JSON: output/gatsby/analysis.json\n- Quality Report: output/gatsby_20260118_135712/quality.md\n\n## Pipeline Notes (Attempt 4)\n- Analysis completed in 65m 42s\n- Total tokens: 706,465\n- Narrator detected: Mrs. Sigourney Howard (CRITICAL ISSUE - still wrong)\n- 59 characters extracted\n- 10 chapters detected\n- Warnings:\n  - TOC validation: 87 entries seems too many\n  - TOC enforcement: Only 9 boundaries found but TOC expects 87\n  - StructureAgent: 8 errors found but refinement not yet implemented\n  - StructureAgent: 5 errors found but refinement not yet implemented\n  - 3 low-confidence character profiles (Sloane, Mr. McKee, Mrs. McKee)\n  - Multiple moral valence classification failures (Gatsby, Tom, Daisy, Myrtle, McKee, Mr. McKee, Mrs. McKee)\n  - LLM server errors (500) during character profiling\n  - JSON parsing failure for Sloane\n  - LLM identity detection failed, evidence extraction failed for Gatsby","originalFile":"# Current Evaluation State\n\n## Active Text\n- **Name:** gatsby\n- **Attempt:** 3 of 5\n- **Phase:** awaiting_evaluation\n- **baseline_score:** 6.20\n\n## Output Files\n- HTML: output/gatsby/report.html\n- JSON: output/gatsby/analysis.json\n- Quality Report: output/gatsby_20260118_124832/quality.md\n\n## Pipeline Notes (Attempt 3)\n- Analysis completed in 64m 16s\n- Total tokens: 698,614\n- Narrator detected: Mrs. Sigourney Howard (CRITICAL ISSUE - still wrong)\n- 60 characters extracted\n- 9 chapters detected\n- Warnings:\n  - TOC validation: 87 entries seems too many\n  - StructureAgent: 2 errors found but refinement not yet implemented\n  - 4 low-confidence character profiles (McKee, Catherine, the butler, Mrs. McKee)\n  - Multiple moral valence classification failures\n  - Multiple JSON parsing failures for character profiles\n\n## Latest Scores\n- Structure Detection: 8/10\n- Character Extraction: 4/10 ← CRITICAL FAILURES\n- Character Profiles: 5/10 ← CRITICAL FAILURE\n- Chapter Summaries: 7/10\n- Pronunciation Guide: 5/10\n- HTML Presentation: 9/10\n- **Overall: 6.05/10** (threshold: 8.0)\n\n### Score Breakdown\n\n**Structure Detection: 8/10**\n- 10 chapters detected (Gatsby has 9 chapters - off by one, likely front matter counted)\n- Chapter numbering is confusing: \"Chapter 7: VI\", \"Chapter 8: VII\", \"Chapter 9: VIII\" mixes Arabic and Roman numerals\n- Chapter boundaries appear mostly correct based on content\n- Chapter summaries align with actual chapter content\n- Minor: Off-by-one chapter count and confusing numbering\n\n**Character Extraction: 4/10** (WORSE than attempt 1)\n- CRITICAL FAILURE: James Gatz (6 mentions, alias \"Mr. Gatz\") is STILL listed separately from Gatsby (257 mentions, alias \"Mr. Gatsby\"). The fix from attempt 1 to the pairwise alias prompt did NOT work.\n- CRITICAL FAILURE: McKee entry STILL shows \"Also known as: Mr. McKee, Mrs. McKee\" - the gendered title fix from attempt 1 did NOT work.\n- Major characters present (Gatsby, Tom, Daisy, Wilson, Jordan Baker, Wolfshiem, Myrtle, Nick)\n- Tom and Daisy Buchanan are correctly kept separate (GOOD)\n- Nick Carraway has only 24 mentions (expected - first-person narrator design limitation)\n\n**Character Profiles: 5/10** (WORSE than attempt 1)\n- CRITICAL FAILURE: Plot summary STILL identifies narrator as \"Mrs. Sigourney Howard\" (lines 631-635 in HTML). The narrator detection fix from attempt 1 COMPLETELY FAILED.\n- Mrs. Sigourney Howard appears in the plot summary 4 times as narrator (\"Mrs. Sigourney Howard, a reflective and observant woman, recounts...\", \"Mrs. Howard becomes increasingly entangled...\", \"Mrs. Howard bears witness...\")\n- Nick Carraway is the actual narrator - Mrs. Sigourney Howard is a minor party guest mentioned ONCE in Chapter 3\n- Character profile descriptions are otherwise reasonable\n- Relationship detection is empty (\"No explicit relationships detected\")\n\n**Chapter Summaries: 7/10**\n- Summaries are detailed and capture key events\n- MEDIUM ERROR: Chapter 9 summary incorrectly states \"the narrator shares a tender, silent afternoon with Daisy before his impending departure, realizing her love for him\" - this should be Jordan Baker, not Daisy. Nick's romantic interest is Jordan, and he is Daisy's cousin.\n- Other summaries appear accurate (Myrtle's death, Plaza confrontation, Gatsby's murder correctly described)\n- Appropriate length (100-400 words per chapter)\n\n**Pronunciation Guide: 5/10** (SLIGHT IMPROVEMENT)\n- 74 proper nouns, 23 homographs, 13 foreign words (reduced from 627 total in attempt 1)\n- Homograph handling is good (house, minute, live, close, read, wind)\n- MEDIUM: False positives STILL present in \"Proper Nouns\" section:\n  - \"man\" (114 occurrences) - common word, NOT a proper noun\n  - \"first\" (56 occurrences) - common word, NOT a proper noun\n  - \"girl\" (48 occurrences) - common word, NOT a proper noun\n  - \"butler\" (20 occurrences) - common word, NOT a proper noun\n  - \"chauffeur\" (18 occurrences) - common word (though legitimate vocabulary)\n- Legitimate proper nouns are present (Wolfshiem, Buchanan, Klipspringer, etc.)\n\n**HTML Presentation: 9/10**\n- Professional, dark-themed design\n- Tab navigation functional\n- Collapsible sections for chapters and evidence\n- Search and filter functionality present\n- Minor: Chapter numbering confusion (Arabic + Roman)\n\n## Score Calculation\n\n```\nOverall = (\n    Structure × 0.20 +     8 × 0.20 = 1.60\n    Characters × 0.25 +    4 × 0.25 = 1.00\n    Profiles × 0.15 +      5 × 0.15 = 0.75\n    Summaries × 0.20 +     7 × 0.20 = 1.40\n    Pronunciation × 0.10 + 5 × 0.10 = 0.50\n    Presentation × 0.10 +  9 × 0.10 = 0.90\n) = 6.15/10\n```\n\n**Overall: 6.15/10** (threshold: 8.0) - FAIL\n\n## Current Issues (Priority Order)\n\n### CRITICAL\n\n1. **Narrator STILL misidentified as Mrs. Sigourney Howard**\n   - **Problem:** Plot summary says \"Mrs. Sigourney Howard, a reflective and observant woman, recounts the summer of 1922...\"\n   - **Evidence:** Nick Carraway is the narrator. Mrs. Sigourney Howard is a minor party guest in Chapter 3.\n   - **Attempt 1 Fix:** Modified `src/pipeline/character_profiling/narrator.py` to sort characters by mention count and added critical rules about minor characters not being narrators\n   - **Why It Failed:** The narrator detection is happening BEFORE the plot summary is generated. The plot summary explicitly uses \"Mrs. Sigourney Howard\" 4 times, suggesting the LLM is hallucinating the narrator name during summary generation, NOT during narrator detection.\n   - **Location:** Likely `src/agents/summary_agent.py` or wherever the plot summary is generated - the narrator name is being inserted into the summary incorrectly\n   - **New Fix Approach:** The fix should be applied to the SUMMARY generation, not narrator detection. Either:\n     a) Pass the detected narrator name to the summary agent and enforce its use\n     b) Post-process the summary to replace incorrect narrator names\n     c) Check if narrator detection is even being used in summary generation\n\n2. **James Gatz / Gatsby STILL separate characters**\n   - **Problem:** \"James Gatz\" (6 mentions, first appears Ch. 7) is listed separately from \"Gatsby\" (257 mentions)\n   - **Evidence:** James Gatz is Jay Gatsby's birth name. Chapter 6 reveals: \"James Gatz—that was really, or at least legally, his name.\"\n   - **Attempt 1 Fix:** Enhanced `PAIRWISE_ALIAS_PROMPT` to mention birth names\n   - **Why It Failed:** The LLM is still rejecting the merge. The prompt enhancement was not sufficient. The issue is likely:\n     a) The pair \"James Gatz\" + \"Gatsby\" may not be generated as candidates\n     b) Or the LLM is still rejecting despite the enhanced prompt\n   - **Location:** `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py`\n   - **New Fix Approach:** Need to either:\n     a) Force-pair names that share \"Gatz/Gatsby\" pattern (fuzzy phonetic matching)\n     b) Add explicit few-shot examples to the prompt showing birth name merges\n     c) Check if the candidate pair is even being generated\n\n3. **Mr. McKee / Mrs. McKee STILL falsely merged**\n   - **Problem:** \"McKee\" entry shows \"Also known as: Mr. McKee, Mrs. McKee\"\n   - **Evidence:** Chapter 2: \"Chester McKee was a pale, feminine man... His wife was shrill, languid...\"\n   - **Attempt 1 Fix:** Added special case check for \"Title LastName\" pairs with gendered titles\n   - **Why It Failed:** The code checks `len(words) == 2` for title+lastname pairs, but the merge validation is happening at the wrong stage or the check is being bypassed\n   - **Location:** `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` (lines 1510-1545)\n   - **New Fix Approach:** Debug why the gendered title check isn't firing. Add logging to trace the exact merge decision for \"Mr. McKee\" + \"Mrs. McKee\"\n\n### HIGH\n\n4. **Chapter 9 Summary Error - Daisy vs Jordan Baker**\n   - **Problem:** Summary says \"the narrator shares a tender, silent afternoon with Daisy... realizing her love for him\"\n   - **Evidence:** Nick's romantic interest is Jordan Baker, not Daisy (his cousin). This scene is about Nick and Jordan.\n   - **Location:** Summary agent LLM generation\n   - **Fix:** Lower temperature or add fact-checking for relationship accuracy\n\n5. **Chapter numbering confusion**\n   - **Problem:** Chapters show \"Chapter 7: VI\", \"Chapter 8: VII\" mixing Arabic and Roman numerals\n   - **Evidence:** Gatsby uses Roman numerals (I-IX). The tool is detecting both formats and concatenating.\n   - **Location:** Structure/chapter detection pipeline\n   - **Fix:** Normalize chapter numbering to one format\n\n### MEDIUM\n\n6. **Pronunciation false positives - common words flagged**\n   - **Problem:** \"man\", \"first\", \"girl\", \"butler\" flagged as proper nouns\n   - **Evidence:** These are common English words appearing in various contexts\n   - **Location:** `src/pipeline/pronunciation/` or pronunciation agent\n   - **Fix:** Add common English word list filter (top 5000-10000 words)\n\n7. **Relationship detection empty**\n   - **Problem:** \"No explicit relationships detected\" for all characters\n   - **Evidence:** Obvious relationships exist: Tom+Daisy (married), Tom+Myrtle (affair), Gatsby+Daisy (lovers), Nick+Jordan (romantic)\n   - **Location:** Character profiling pipeline\n   - **Fix:** Implement or improve relationship extraction\n\n## Fix History\n\n### Attempt 1 Fixes (Applied but FAILED)\n\n**Fix 1: James Gatz / Gatsby birth name merge** ❌ FAILED\n- Modified: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` (line 104-138)\n- Change: Enhanced PAIRWISE_ALIAS_PROMPT to mention birth names\n- Result: James Gatz STILL separate from Gatsby\n\n**Fix 2: Narrator misidentification** ❌ FAILED\n- Modified: `src/pipeline/character_profiling/narrator.py` (lines 70-100, 137-150)\n- Change: Enhanced narrator detection prompt, sorted characters by mention count\n- Result: Plot summary STILL uses Mrs. Sigourney Howard as narrator\n\n**Fix 3: Mr. McKee / Mrs. McKee false merge** ❌ FAILED\n- Modified: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` (lines 1510-1545)\n- Change: Added gendered title check for Title+LastName pairs\n- Result: McKee STILL shows both Mr. and Mrs. as aliases\n\n### Attempt 2 Fixes (NEW)\n\n**Fix 1: Narrator hallucination in plot summary** 🔧 APPLIED\n- Modified: `src/pipeline/overview/generator.py` (lines 17-30)\n- Change: Added CRITICAL constraints to PLOT_SUMMARY_SYSTEM prompt to prevent narrator name hallucination\n- Rationale: Attempt 1 fixed narrator DETECTION, but the plot summary is generated BEFORE narrator detection runs. The LLM was hallucinating narrator names from chapter summaries. Added explicit system-level constraints: \"Do NOT invent, assume, or infer narrator names\" and \"write the plot summary WITHOUT mentioning who is narrating\" if narrator not explicitly provided.\n- Expected Impact: Plot summary should no longer mention \"Mrs. Sigourney Howard\" as narrator\n\n**Fix 2: James Gatz / Gatsby phonetic similarity pairing** 🔧 APPLIED\n- Modified: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` (lines 910-958)\n- Change: Added phonetic last-name similarity pairing using difflib.SequenceMatcher (60% threshold)\n- Rationale: Attempt 1 enhanced the LLM prompt, but \"James Gatz\" and \"Gatsby\" were never generated as a candidate pair because they share no words or substrings. The LLM can't merge what it never evaluates. Added new pairing strategy to catch phonetically similar last names (\"gatz\" vs \"gatsby\" = 0.67 similarity).\n- Expected Impact: \"James Gatz\" and \"Gatsby\" should now be paired, evaluated by LLM, and merged\n\n**Fix 3: McKee gendered title conflict (global check)** 🔧 APPLIED\n- Modified: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` (lines 1565-1610)\n- Change: Added global check for opposite-gendered variants before merging bare last name + titled version\n- Rationale: Attempt 1 added pairwise check for \"Mr. McKee\" vs \"Mrs. McKee\", but they were being merged separately to \"McKee\" (bare last name). When validating \"McKee\" + \"Mrs. McKee\", the code didn't check if \"Mr. McKee\" already existed. Added check to scan all names in name_groups for opposite-gendered variants of the same last name before allowing merge.\n- Expected Impact: \"McKee\" should NOT merge with both \"Mr. McKee\" and \"Mrs. McKee\" - one will be rejected\n\n## Regression Check\n- **baseline_score:** 6.20 (from attempt 1)\n- **new_score:** 6.15\n- **difference:** -0.05 (within tolerance, no regression)\n\n## Next Action\n\n**Phase:** awaiting_analysis\n\nRe-run analysis with attempt 2 fixes to verify improvements.\n\n**Fixes Applied:** 3 CRITICAL issues addressed (all from Character Extraction/Profiles category)\n- Narrator hallucination in plot summary (system prompt constraints)\n- James Gatz / Gatsby merge (phonetic pairing)\n- McKee gendered title conflict (global validation)\n\n**Expected Improvements:**\n- Character Profiles score should improve from 5/10 to 7-8/10 (narrator fix)\n- Character Extraction score should improve from 4/10 to 6-7/10 (Gatz/Gatsby merge, McKee fix)\n- Overall score expected: 6.15 → 7.0-7.5 (still below 8.0 threshold, but significant progress)\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":27,"newStart":2,"newLines":31,"lines":[" "," ## Active Text"," - **Name:** gatsby","-- **Attempt:** 3 of 5","+- **Attempt:** 4 of 5"," - **Phase:** awaiting_evaluation"," - **baseline_score:** 6.20"," "," ## Output Files"," - HTML: output/gatsby/report.html"," - JSON: output/gatsby/analysis.json","-- Quality Report: output/gatsby_20260118_124832/quality.md","+- Quality Report: output/gatsby_20260118_135712/quality.md"," ","-## Pipeline Notes (Attempt 3)","-- Analysis completed in 64m 16s","-- Total tokens: 698,614","+## Pipeline Notes (Attempt 4)","+- Analysis completed in 65m 42s","+- Total tokens: 706,465"," - Narrator detected: Mrs. Sigourney Howard (CRITICAL ISSUE - still wrong)","-- 60 characters extracted","-- 9 chapters detected","+- 59 characters extracted","+- 10 chapters detected"," - Warnings:","   - TOC validation: 87 entries seems too many","-  - StructureAgent: 2 errors found but refinement not yet implemented","-  - 4 low-confidence character profiles (McKee, Catherine, the butler, Mrs. McKee)","-  - Multiple moral valence classification failures","-  - Multiple JSON parsing failures for character profiles","+  - TOC enforcement: Only 9 boundaries found but TOC expects 87","+  - StructureAgent: 8 errors found but refinement not yet implemented","+  - StructureAgent: 5 errors found but refinement not yet implemented","+  - 3 low-confidence character profiles (Sloane, Mr. McKee, Mrs. McKee)","+  - Multiple moral valence classification failures (Gatsby, Tom, Daisy, Myrtle, McKee, Mr. McKee, Mrs. McKee)","+  - LLM server errors (500) during character profiling","+  - JSON parsing failure for Sloane","+  - LLM identity detection failed, evidence extraction failed for Gatsby"," "," ## Latest Scores"," - Structure Detection: 8/10"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
